kind: llman.sdd.spec
name: "governance-docs-site"
purpose: "定义仓库内文档站点的范围与组织规则：使用 Zensical（兼容 MkDocs 的配置格式）构建站点，以 `docs/doc/` 作为唯一文档真源，避免将规范、审计报告等纳入站点。 [scope-review-2026-07-12-c5-openpyxl-helpers]"
valid_scope[1]: src/scalim/
requirements[5]{req_id,title,statement}:
  r1,Documentation site is properly configured,The system MUST provide a Zensical configuration and treat `docs/doc/` as the canonical documentation root.
  r2,"Site scope excludes non-manual content","The system MUST exclude third-party artifacts and non-manual content (specs, audit reports) from the documentation site. Repository-owned generated docs MAY be included if drift-checked."
  r3,Legacy docs are migrated and removed,The system MUST migrate reorganized legacy docs into the canonical documentation root and remove originals to avoid duplicate sources of truth.
  r4,Tutorial entry page for demo_big_data_report,"The system MUST provide a discoverable tutorial entry page under `docs/doc/` that links to the marimo tutorial, `just examples` command, and YAML DSL canonical example. The page MUST declare doc governance boundaries (hand-maintained vs generated content, and CI gates)."
  r5,YAML DSL manual pages reflect current implementation,"The system MUST ensure YAML DSL manual pages stay consistent with implementation to avoid “docs say X but code rejects it” drift. Manual pages MUST NOT present removed syntax as valid and MUST accurately describe current imports/outputs behavior. Key manual pages include: syntax reference, capability matrix, and user guide. Manual pages MUST: - NOT recommend removed workbook container output syntax - Clarify legacy `outputs.*.container` removal and current CSV output binding method - Describe Excel output binding through resources.books - Accurately describe imports/$import path resolution without conflicting with implementation"
scenarios[13]{req_id,id,given,when,then}:
  r1,baseline,"","TODO: describe the trigger","TODO: describe the expected result"
  r1,"build-succeeds","",a developer runs the docs build command,the build MUST complete successfully
  r1,"docs-root-is-configured","",the documentation site is configured,the configured docs directory MUST resolve to the canonical documentation root
  r2,baseline,"","TODO: describe the trigger","TODO: describe the expected result"
  r2,"site-content-stays-curated","",the documentation site is built or served,only curated pages and explicitly allowed generated pages are included
  r3,baseline,"","TODO: describe the trigger","TODO: describe the expected result"
  r3,"old-paths-are-removed","",a reader opens an old file path that has been reorganized,the file MUST no longer exist at the old path
  r4,baseline,"","TODO: describe the trigger","TODO: describe the expected result"
  r4,"entry-page-is-discoverable-from-reading-guide","",a reader opens the reading guide,the document MUST contain a link to the tutorial entry page
  r4,"entry-page-is-discoverable-from-yaml-dsl-manual","",a reader opens the YAML DSL manual index,the document MUST contain a link to the tutorial entry page
  r5,baseline,"","TODO: describe the trigger","TODO: describe the expected result"
  r5,"user-guide-does-not-recommend-removed-syntax","",a reader follows the user guide outputs examples,the examples MUST NOT include removed workbook container output syntax
  r5,"manual-describes-legacy-removal-and-current-bindings","",a reader reviews outputs sections,the documentation MUST describe legacy removal and current output binding methods for CSV and Excel